        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(telegram): add MCP App Funnel proof fixture",
        "body": "Related: #111211\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe trusted real-user Telegram Desktop capture could not configure the official MCP App fixture or publish the Gateway origin required to prove a native Mini App button end to end.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds one opt-in `--mcp-app-fixture` session mode. It provisions a fresh Tailscale-enabled Crabbox desktop lease, lets the real Gateway own Funnel through a narrow SSH CLI bridge and reverse tunnel, serves the pinned official SDK fixture, and explicitly resets Funnel during teardown. Existing Telegram proof sessions are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo product behavior changes. Maintainers can capture the full Telegram MCP App user path in the protected Mantis workflow without exposing Tailscale credentials or leaving a public route behind.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I understand and reviewed the implementation. A redacted agent transcript was not inserted because approval was requested but not granted.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/telegram-user-crabbox-proof.test.ts test/scripts/e2e-mock-config-limits.test.ts test/scripts/mantis-telegram-desktop-proof-workflow.test.ts` — 65 passed\n- Fresh branch autoreview against `upstream/main` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n- Exact pre-push base: `6eb569ed6ef2686250d413a144c39b26a19dc4a5`\n- The protected Telegram credential lease is available only in GitHub QA; exact live Mantis proof will run after this prerequisite lands and #111211 merges the resulting main commit.\n",
